\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Lemma}
\title{Unequal reverse weights obstruct one form}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{Suppose the edges #{x\to y} and #{y\to x} are both present and
one identifies them. A single weight for the identified edge
agrees with both derived weights if and only if those weights
are equal. Their difference is the obstruction to that
identification, and that obstruction is not developed further.}

\proof{
\p{Under the identification the two edges become one vector.
\ref{fdip-00PB} assigns #{L_{xy}} to the first and #{L_{yx}}
to the second. One quadratic value on that vector equals both
assignments exactly when #{L_{xy}=L_{yx}}. The difference of
the two weights is zero exactly in that case.}
}
